  "id": "Compound::DB00356 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Chlorzoxazone exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2d6 and Cyp2a6, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are part of the cytochrome P450 system, and their participation in the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid is a well-documented pathway. The evidence suggests that Chlorzoxazone may influence the activity of Cyp2e1 through its interaction with Cyp2d6 and Cyp2a6, which in turn modulate the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid. This mechanism implies that Chlorzoxazone could affect the metabolic pathways involving arachidonic acid, potentially influencing the production of pro-inflammatory mediators. The consistent binding and participation relationships across the three paths indicate a plausible, mechanistically linked interaction between Chlorzoxazone and Cyp2e1, supported by the shared role of these enzymes in arachidonic acid metabolism. The evidence is robust and aligns with established biochemical pathways, suggesting a direct and biologically relevant relationship.",
